Short:        Lightweight high-performance TCP/IP stack & bsdsocket.library
Author:       Tolon
Uploader:     tolon
Type:         comm/tcp
Version:      1.0.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0

==============================================================================
tolunnet — Lightweight High-Performance TCP/IP Network Stack for AmigaOS
==============================================================================

tolunnet is a modern, lightweight, high-performance TCP/IP network stack and
bsdsocket.library v4.1 runtime designed specifically for Motorola 68020+
Commodore Amiga systems running AmigaOS 3.0 or later.

Features:
- Single-task cooperative architecture (lwIP 2.2.0 NO_SYS=1)
- Zero-allocation Exec IPC messaging over "tolunnet.port"
- Standard bsdsocket.library v4.1 compatible with AmiTCP and Roadshow applications
- Complete IPv4, ARP, ICMP Echo, UDP (SOCK_DGRAM), TCP (SOCK_STREAM), DNS client
- Built-in DHCP client with automatic lease configuration
- Hardware-seeded entropy PRNG (GetSysTime, MAC, memory pools)
- Fast 68k assembly register trampolines for SANA-II Rev 7 buffer management
- Diagnostic tools: TolunnetPing, TolunnetGet, TolunnetStatus
- Standard Commodore Installer script & AmigaGuide documentation

Requirements:
- Commodore Amiga (A500/A600/A1200/A2000/A3000/A4000) or WinUAE / FS-UAE
- Motorola 68020 CPU or higher (68030, 68040, 68060, PiStorm)
- AmigaOS 3.0 or later
- Standard SANA-II network device driver

Installation:
Double-click on the "Install_Tolunnet" icon or copy binaries in C/ to SYS:C/.
See README.guide for complete details.
